I'd like to work on this if nobody has picked it up.

On main `8bb3e702`, I independently reproduced the `ParamWrapper` forward failure with two real CPU/Gloo ranks and an expert-axis sharded DTensor parameter. Dense LoRA completes forward/backward with adapter gradients, and the expert-sharded base model without LoRA also works. Combining them fails on both ranks with the reported mixed Tensor/DTensor `baddbmm` error. This isolates the parameter-wrapper path; it is not validation of the full Transformers TP/EP loader or GPU training setup.

Proposed scope, building on rather than duplicating #3838:
- align expert LoRA factors with the base parameter's EP/TP placements and shape semantics, without gathering the full expert weight as a workaround;
- add distributed versus unsharded forward/gradient equivalence and adapter save/load regressions, preserving ordinary `target_parameters` behavior;
- focus on TP/EP first; treat combined FSDP as a follow-up unless you prefer it in the initial

@maintainer-2 Thanks for reporting, we indeed have a gap here.

@user-4 Please feel free to give it a try. If you want, open a draft PR so we can discuss designs if there is uncertainty. Let's assume that #3838 will be merged.

/peft-triage approved
